  "id": "natural-family-planning",
  "term": "natural family planning",
  "definition": "Natural family planning is a family-planning approach that uses signs of potential fertility during the menstrual cycle, such as bodily biomarkers, to identify times when intercourse is more likely to lead to pregnancy. Couples can use this information to adjust sexual behavior depending on whether they want to avoid pregnancy or conceive.",
